# Geometry

- Coordinates: origin at wall × top of lower shelf; +X into the room; +Y up; millimeters.
- Model the LED as a segment (or thin rectangle) of `led.width`. Sample ends plus ≥16 interior points.
- Mount types are distinct: `corner` (angled emit at the wall/shelf corner) and `downward` (horizontal emit under the upper shelf).
- Occluders are solid bodies: upper shelf, lower shelf, valance (бленда). Edge graze counts as blocked.
- Direct glare exists if any emit-point → eye segment is unobstructed and in the emitter's front half-plane.
- Do not replace the segment test with a single worst-case point. The inner edge can glare when looking up under the shelf.
